  From anywhere, privately

  ╭──────────────────╮      ╭─────────────────╮      ╭───────────────╮
  │ your phone or    │──────│ Tailscale       │──────│ this computer │
  │ laptop, anywhere │      │ private network │      │ private name  │
  ╰──────────────────╯      ╰────────┬────────╯      ╰───────────────╯
                               private names

  Tailscale lets you open each App with its own private HTTPS name from your phone, laptop or TV,
  wherever you are. Existing IP:port Addresses and firewall rules stay unchanged.

  What is Tailscale?
  A service that joins your own devices into one private network, wherever they are. Access to
  Tailscale Addresses follows your Tailscale access rules. Existing IP:port Addresses are
  separate.

  On your phone or TV
  Install Tailscale on your phone, laptop or TV and sign in to the same account. Apple TV and
  Android TV have apps; other TVs may need the Home network Address.

  Turn on HTTPS
  Open https://login.tailscale.com/admin/dns, check MagicDNS is on and enable HTTPS. App names
  will appear in a public certificate log. This publishes the names, not access to your Apps.


